ormation for albertans on if  we could see this happen could surgeries  be postponed could procedures be  postponed and and how are we going to  staff this if we do get to that level  unfortunately again that the details of  staffing aren't things i could comment  on but it is absolutely clear that as  the burden of acute care  rises with respect to coveted missions  that postponement of surgeries or other  procedures that are non-urgent  is absolutely something that  is possible as the system makes space  for the need to care for patients who  who have covid and again even those who  are admitted for other reasons  but have a covet infection  need to have additional protocols to  prevent spread of infection so there are  still impacts in terms of capacity even  with those patients so again  absolutely there could be an impact on  surgeries and other procedures  the details unfortunately would have to  be something ahs could comment on  lauren do you have a follow-up  i do thank you  we are now uh in the fifth wave of this  uh we have hit record hospitalizations  during the fourth wave as well can you  explain to me how did we get to this  point again and do you take any  responsibility for what led us here  i think that one of the major factors is  the high transmissibility of the omicron  variant  the question about the progression of  the wave certainly in every wave we've  had  we've seen  a  series of  points in time where the situation is  assessed  i have provided  recommendations along the way  and so the the decisions about  managing cases managing the wave i can't  speak  on behalf of elected officials about  decisions all i can say is that  omicron is more challenging than  anything we have dealt with before that  it is more transmissible it does cause  more breakthrough infections  and that  the decisions about managing that  pressure again are not mine to make  operator please put through the next  caller  dylan short post media  hi dr hinshaw looking a